title: 'C5''a: per-server trust and brokered Always rules (kernel)'
summary: |-
  Aegis owned the design of C5'. The founder's answers:
  - repo/local servers stay out of local sessions;
  - no Always for untrusted servers;
  - one tool per rule, no expiry, a rule pauses when its binding changes;
  - standing grants can create rules.

  Arky's review added 11 amendments and split the work.

  C5'a1 (trust):
  - trust lives in kernel-signed tool.trust rows (TrustBook); the store's trust field is never read;
  - trust is bound to the keyed launch hash, pluginVersion and toolsHash, and drops with a row;
  - request.mcp.trust is preview then commit.
  - Aegis H1: commit had no fresh press. It now raises a root+presence grant card that is never standing and hand-only.
  - Merged e5eaf815.

  C5'a2 (rules):
  - the 'tool' approve scope;
  - the bindHash taken from the request row inside the contentHash;
  - the rule pass for mutate tools on live-trust servers only, with RULED_PER_MINUTE 20;
  - portal ^local-tool-grant;
  - G-LCL-22, G-LCL-23;
  - one trust card per server, replaced when the listing changes.
  - Aegis signed off.

  Merged and pushed. The full gnomon suite: 4195 passed, 0 failed.
symbols_touched:
  - ^local-tool-grant
  - '#mcp-servers'
  - '#local-tool-broker'
  - '#local-mcp-client'
  - '#always-rules'
decisions:
  - id: c5-repo-servers-out
    decision: Project/local MCP servers stay out of local sessions until they have their own approval step
    rationale: A cloned repo could choose a server command; founder agreed with Aegis
  - id: c5-trust-fresh-press
    decision: Trusting a server needs a fresh root+presence card, never standing, never voice
    rationale: 'Founder: trusting always needs a fresh press; Aegis H1'
  - id: c5-rule-shape
    decision: Always rule = one tool on one trusted server in one repo, no expiry, dormant on a binding change; never destructive
    rationale: Founder choice; the narrowest rule that removes repeat cards
learnings:
  - A design that says 'like X' about who may call should also say whether presence is needed; Aegis's own brief caused H1.
  - Builders reliably hit the 100-turn limit on kernel slices with 10+ files; split slices at about 8 source files, or plan a resume.
